  "contract": [
    "Native SpO2 deinit accepts a null owner. Otherwise reload it before each of six nested destructors and final free, then clear it unconditionally after free and return success.",
    "Preserve unconditional versus guarded releases, individual cell-clear timing, live aggregate/owned/buffer roots and the separate300-offset context-pair child. Do not add null-record guards where stock dereferences records.",
    "The channel-array gate is descriptor+1c. Each loop check reads the current unsigned descriptor count and current array root, including the terminating check. Release-clear entry+14 at40-byte stride, then free the current root.",
    "The public HR/SpO2 adapters ignore their frame and normalize any full-word nonzero parent status to-1. Existing HR processing teardown and every SpO2 descendant execute in actual C heap integration."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "All606 native instruction bytes execute:570 in SpO2/descendant/shared-cell paths and36 in public status adapters. Direct tests model free or parent status; integration executes the actual C allocator and all descendant bodies without entering stock code.",
    "Direct fixtures cover every nullable field individually, masks, gates and bounded counts0/1/4, plus live count growth/shrinkage and high unsigned counts terminated by a callback count change. They do not claim exhaustive arbitrary descriptor sizes or concurrency.",
    "Sixteen null-argument cases distinguish the three supported null paths from thirteen initial unmapped reads in the emulator. These are access-shape checks, not claims of a physical MCU fault.",
    "Saved integer/FP registers, SP, interrupt masks, FPSCR, guards and full heap write width/order/values checked. Caller scratch, APSR and private stack frames excluded.",
    "One canonical four-byte SpO2 owner added for future initialization to share. Typed fixture construction is not recovered algorithm initialization. ADT/soft ADT shutdown, controller, initialization/computation, physical sensors, final executable linking/startup and boot remain open. Relocatable composition is not bootable firmware."
  ],
